  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry through tonight. Daily rainfall chances begin this\nweekend and continue through early next week. \n\nHigh pressure will remain over the area through tonight and\nprovide a nice evening for outdoor activities. \n\nBy Saturday, advection of moisture ahead of an approaching\nclosed upper level low will bring increasing clouds along with\nthe chance for afternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms.\nThis low is progged to be slow moving and it is forecast to\nlinger for several days, resulting in scattered to numerous\nshowers and thunderstorms (both nocturnal and diurnal) for the \nlatter half of the weekend and into early next week. \n\nOverall, pattern is not supportive of organized severe, but \nrepetitive slow moving showers and thunderstorms may begin to \nincrease hydro concerns. Precipitable Water values (approaching\n2 inches) gives some confidence in this as well. Temperatures \nnext week generally at or slightly below normal.",
